{
  "narrative": "All twelve new discovery analyses are valid and have adequate cell counts, but none has a 95% interval excluding zero. Using an approximate clinical benchmark of 10% of the absolute outcome mean, feature_060 does not show a coherent dependency-enhancing main-effect pattern across the outcome panel. For outcome_005, outcome_012, outcome_004, outcome_015, outcome_002, outcome_003, outcome_010, and outcome_016, the signed confidence bounds in the hypothesized direction are below the approximate 10% threshold or the estimates are opposite the registered direction, so I reject H14, H15, H17, H25, H26, H27, H28, and H29 as not supported in this dataset. outcome_014 is an exception only because its absolute mean is small and the interval is wide; H24 remains unresolved but deferred. The feature_002 main effects on outcome_007 and outcome_009 are clinically unmeaningfully small, so H16 and H18 are rejected. The only candidate worth following is H23: the feature_060 by feature_034 interaction on outcome_006 has a large positive signed estimate (+0.0488, about 5x the approximate outcome_006 threshold), but its interval crosses zero and arose in an exploratory scan with substantial multiplicity. I do not accept it based on discovery alone, but it is the most promising eligible claim, so I request independent validation for H23. I also register direct follow-up comparisons for the subgroup variable and simple effects within feature_034=1 and feature_034=0 to characterize whether the interaction is real or an artifact of a null main effect. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "After iteration 2 discovery batch: feature_060 main-effect replication largely fails. H14 reject (upper bound below threshold for outcome_005); H15 reject (opposite/small); H17 reject; H24 unresolved/deferred because outcome_014 has small threshold and wide CI; H25-H29 reject. feature_002: H16/H18 reject. H13 remains unresolved but not validated because the original main effect is imprecise and main-effect convergence is poor. H23 outcome_006 interaction estimate +0.0488 with wide CI; only claim with CI spanning large clinically meaningful positive values, so validation requested for H23. Next: analyze H23 validation and registered simple-effect/main-effect characterizations if needed; if validation is null, reject/close subgroup candidate and return to broader categorical/binary exploration (H19-H22 etc).",
